The first excited state follows by raising the ground state: $\psi_{1}(x)\propto A_{+}\psi_{0}(x)
\propto(p+i\omega x)e^{-\omega x^{2}/2}.$ The ground-state equation says $p\psi_{0}=i\omega x\,\psi_{0}.$ Changing the sign in the ladder operator turns the cancellation into addition: $(p+i\omega x)\psi_{0}
=2i\omega x\,\psi_{0}.$ Up to an overall constant, $\psi_{1}(x)\propto x\,e^{-\omega x^{2}/2}.$

